{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 560,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An apple weighs about 1 newton, the world record for jet engine thrust is 570,000 newtons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7760,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the Saturn V rocket that launched people to the moon had a thrust of 33,360,000 newtons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14660,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how can we measure forces this big accurately?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18940,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we need to ask this guy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20540,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hi my name is Rick Seifarth I'm a physical\nscientist in the Mass and Force Group."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24660,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Am I supposed to look at the camera?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25880,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26440,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26940,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can look at anything you like."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28780,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rick manages a dead weight machine \nthat can apply 4,448,222 newtons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35060,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why such a strange number? Because that's\nexactly equal to 1,000,000 pounds of force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41060,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are twenty fifty thousand\npound increments in this machine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44380,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20 times 50 equals 1,000,000 pounds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46800,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cumulatively that's 4.45 mega newton."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49940,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Elsewhere in the world, are there larger \nmasses that people have calibrated?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53440,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I ask that question to every visitor\nwe get and I've not gotten.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56980,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one response that says: yeah I know \nwhere bigger stuff is calibrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60800,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I really want to go out\non a limb and brag I'll say"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63260,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these are the largest mass objects ever calibrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66940,
    "dDurationMs": 540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anywhere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68460,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The machine works like this, below ground \nare the 20 carefully calibrated masses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73400,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their weight is used to calibrate\nforce sensors also called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Force Transducers, in the lab upstairs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83260,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a one million pound capacity 4.45 mega newton,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86420,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is 13.3 mega newtons,\nthree million pounds force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90440,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the biggest machine of it's type \nin the world, and obviously one of a kind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95340,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of these,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will be placed on the compression head right here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99640,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, a hydraulic ram in the attic starts to raise the green lifting frame"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105380,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once the force transducer \ncontacts the red loading frame,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108880,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then it starts lifting the weights downstairs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112300,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as the lifting frame continues\nto rise, more and more of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115700,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "50,000 pound weights become \nsuspended by the force sensor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119500,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since the weights create an \naccurately-known force,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122480,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the readouts from the force transducer \ncan be precisely calibrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126100,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These devices are then sent out into the field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128880,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well literally, there's a test stand that's\nset up with one of these gizmos-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132900,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a force transducers - embedded\nin the test stand somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144100,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the rocket is fired up, perhaps ramped up, ramped down and those forces are monitored."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148740,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, in the old movies you'd hear: \"go to 104% of power.\" Well, how do they know it's 104% of power?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153800,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because somebody's measured it somewhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155560,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to minimizing uncertainty, these guys aren't messing around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159680,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This piece right here is approximately 50,036.27 pounds of mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165860,
    "dDurationMs": 740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Approximately."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166600,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Approximately, yes! [laughter]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169320,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about that for a moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170640,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of these pieces has a mass equivalent to ten minivans,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174320,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their exact value is known to within several American nickels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179420,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just a few American nickels worth of difference?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182980,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183480,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That tiny uncertainty is measured with respect to the very definition of the kilogram"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188580,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "using K20 - that's the United States fundamental mass standard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193240,
    "dDurationMs": 6260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is done by comparing combinations of known weights, starting with K20, with larger unknown weights,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199500,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gradually working up to larger and larger masses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202340,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, here a single 5-kilogram mass is compared to two 2s and a 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207360,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At some point in this process, they convert and start working in pounds, going from 50-pound masses to 500 pounds,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213840,
    "dDurationMs": 7460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then 2500 pounds. And then, using a scale in the floor, to reach 10,000 pounds and then 20,000,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221360,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and finally 30,000 pounds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224260,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Combinations of these huge weights are then used to calibrate the 50,000-pound masses which form the weight stack."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230280,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we have to have that, because what we sell is the vertical force vector that's generated by these weights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236640,
    "dDurationMs": 7700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hanging in a gravitational field. We sell that with an uncertainty attached to it of 0.0005%,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244340,
    "dDurationMs": 7960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "five parts per million, so that means at full one million pounds of applied force, we guarantee that to be accurate - if you will -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252300,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within five pounds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253500,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not only does that mean the masses have to be accurately calibrated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256640,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it also means the gravitational acceleration at this location has to be taken into account."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261060,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually slightly less than Earth's standard gravity, so an additional 600 pounds are required."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266920,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, the buoyant force must be counteracted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since these masses displace 125 pounds of air,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273560,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a further 125 pounds must be added to reach a million pounds of force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279100,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What strikes me as kind of amazing is that, like, this machine needs to exist, in a way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I would have thought about it, like how would Boeing measure its forces, I would have thought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289540,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OK, they just, you know, calibrate a device that works up to X but then they can, you know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295860,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "generalize. Well, generalize - you know what I mean, like - Yes!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298900,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's an axiom that says \"one physical test is worth a thousand expert opinions.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306500,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that has proven itself time and again, particularly in the world of physical testing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're getting on an airplane that somebody has built, are you willing to accept a 10% uncertainty on these numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316240,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or do you want it to be - the uncertainty on these measurements to be down in the mud?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
